We can choose an assembly variant with `read --variant NAME`, so converted packages contain the parts fitted in that assembly.

We carry Altium project variants through project, explicit project, and adjacent-project opening. We omit not-fitted parts and their owned silkscreen texts, apply changed comments before Altium text resolution, and report retained base-value text when it was already expanded. KiCad DNP parts are omitted by default; a variant can explicitly fit them. Conflicting fitted lists favor not-fitted with a Degraded note.

The manifest always includes `variants` and includes `variant` when selected. Unknown names return a JSON error listing the choices. We keep `info --json` unchanged. Tests cover the numbers and flags recorded in the existing CC0 Altium variants-project and KiCad k10-dnp boards, plus text ownership, changed values, and conflicts. Existing fixture expectations are unchanged.

